{"type":"message","id":"ba1f3474","parentId":"6f953574","timestamp":"2026-07-28T11:35:25.168Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Friction & Turn-Reduction Report — Feed Drain Run (2026-07-28 07:01 UTC)\n\n---\n\n## 1. Turn Count Breakdown\n\n**Total LLM turns: 11** (including the final report request)\n\n| Turn | Tool Calls | Purpose |\n|------|------------|---------|\n| 1 | `exec` (claim feed job) | Claim FEED_JOB_ID=98 |\n| 2 | `exec` (init_run.sh) + variable dumps | Initialize run bundle |\n| 3 | `exec` (update manifest target/pick_run_id) | Step 0.5 — set batch config |\n| 4 | `exec` (build_picker_input.py) | Build picker input with --feed-job-id |\n| 5 | `sessions_spawn(picker)` + `sessions_yield` | Spawn picker subagent |\n| 6 | `exec` (validate_picks.py) | Validate picker output → PICKS_VALID |\n| 7 | `exec` (switch_iteration + update_pick_status) | Start iteration 1 |\n| 8 | `sessions_spawn(researcher)` + `sessions_yield` | Spawn researcher subagent |\n| 9 | `exec` (validate_research + check_duplicates) | Validate research → RESEARCH_VALID |\n| 10 | `exec` (register_topic + verify_artifacts + manifest_step) | Pre-write artifact checks |\n| 11 | `sessions_spawn(writer)` + `sessions_yield` | Spawn writer subagent |\n| 12 | `exec` (verify_artifacts + sync_article + autofix + check_article) | Validate article → ARTICLE_CHECK: PASS |\n| 13 | `exec` (verify_artifacts + manifest_step write) | Post-sync artifact verification |\n| 14 | `exec` (build_creator_input.py) | Build creator input |\n| 15 | `sessions_spawn(creator)` + `sessions_yield` | Spawn creator subagent |\n| 16 | `exec` (ls -lh feature.jpg) | Check image file existence |\n| 17 | `exec` (copy watermarked image from creator run dir) | Fix: creator wrote to wrong path |\n| 18 | `exec` (manifest_step image) | Mark image step succeeded |\n| 19 | `exec` (pandoc + Drive upload) | Step 2.4 — Drive upload |\n| 20 | `exec` (update_manifest_step drive) | Mark drive step succeeded |\n| 21 | `exec` (verify_artifacts pre_wp) | Pre-WP artifact check |\n| 22 | `exec` (publish.sh with image) | First publish attempt → WATERMARK error |\n| 23 | `exec` (copy .watermarked marker) | Fix: copy marker file |\n| 24 | `exec` (publish.sh retry) → `process(poll)` | Retry publish → SUCCESS |\n| 25 | `exec` (update_recent_topics + manifest_step) | Mark drafted status |\n| 26 | `exec` (aggregate_run_tokens) | Aggregate token usage |\n| 27 | `exec` (build_and_send_card.py) | Send news card to Telegram |\n| 28 | `exec` (update_pick_status + switch_iteration --archive) | Mark pick published, archive iteration |\n| 29 | `exec` (cleanup + mark_feed_job + clear_lease + dispatch) | Cleanup and dispatch next jobs |\n| 30 | — | Final friction report request (current turn) |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Compound Execution Opportunities\n\n### High-Impact Chains\n\n| Current Separate Turns | Combined Command | Turns Saved |\n|------------------------|------------------|-------------|\n| Turns 2-3: init_run.sh + manifest update + target/pick_run_id | `init_run.sh && source env && python3 update_manifest_batch.py` | 2 |\n| Turns 9-10: validate_research + check_duplicates + register_topic + verify_artifacts + manifest_step | `validate_research.py && check_recent_topic_duplicates.py && update_recent_topics.py && verify_artifacts.py && update_manifest_step.sh` | 4 |\n| Turns 12-13: verify_artifacts + sync_article + autofix + check_article + manifest_step | `verify_artifacts.py && sync_article_from_raw.py && autofix_article.py && check_article.py && update_manifest_step.sh` | 4 |\n| Turns 25-28: update_recent_topics + manifest_step + aggregate_tokens + send_card + update_pick_status | All sequential Python/bash calls can chain | 3 |\n\n### **Potential Total Turn Reduction: ~13 turns**\n\nIf all safe chains were combined, the orchestrator could complete the full drain run in **~16-17 turns** instead of 30.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Subagent Handoff & Retry Friction\n\n### Subagent Failures: None\n\n| Subagent | Validation Result | Retry Required? |\n|----------|-------------------|-----------------|\n| `picker` | PICKS_VALID (immediate) | No |\n| `researcher` | RESEARCH_VALID (immediate) | No |\n| `writer` | ARTICLE_CHECK: PASS (immediate) | No |\n| `creator` | SUCCESS (but path mismatch) | No |\n\n### Path Mismatch Issue (Creator)\n\n- **Problem:** Creator subagent wrote `feature.jpg` to its **own** run dir (`/tmp/coinography-run-20260728-070600-.../media/`) instead of the **parent orchestrator's** run dir (`/tmp/coinography-run-20260728-070140-.../media/`).\n- **Resolution:** Turns 16-18 manually copied the file and `.watermarked` marker.\n- **Root Cause:** Creator prompt specified `SAVE_TO: /tmp/.../media/feature.jpg` but the subagent's workspace was its own isolated run dir, not the parent's.\n\n**Recommendation:** Creator skill should accept `RUN_DIR` or absolute `OUTPUT_PATH` environment variable and write directly there, or orchestrator should parse the returned path and copy immediately in a single turn.\n\n---\n\n## 4. File Path & Variable Resolution Errors\n\n| Error | Cause | Resolution |\n|-------|--------|------------|\n| Manifest update with literal `$PICK_RUN_ID` | Bash variable not expanded inside heredoc Python block | Direct embed of `RUN_ID` value in Python string |\n| Empty `feature.jpg` (0 bytes) | Creator wrote to its own run dir; orchestrator's path had stale empty file | Copied from creator's run dir |\n| Missing `.watermarked` marker | Marker file not copied with image | Turn 23 copied `.watermarked` marker |\n| First WP publish failed (WATERMARK error) | Publish script refused to upload image without `.watermarked` marker | Turn 23 fixed; retry succeeded |\n\n---\n\n## 5. Top 3 Turn-Reduction Recommendations\n\n### ✅ Recommendation 1: Chain All Validation Scripts Per Stage\n\n**Current:** 6 separate `exec` turns for validation chains (research, article, drive, wp).\n\n**Proposed:**\n```bash\n# Step 2.1: Research validation chain (single turn)\npython3 validate_research.py --manifest \"$PIPELINE_MANIFEST\" --picks \"$RUN_DIR/picker/picks.json\" --pick-index $PICK_INDEX && \\\npython3 check_recent_topic_duplicates.py --current \"$RUN_DIR/research/validated.json\" --registry ~/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator/state/recent_topics.json --window-hours 24 && \\\npython3 update_recent_topics.py --current \"$RUN_DIR/research/validated.json\" --registry ~/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator/state/recent_topics.json --run-id \"$RUN_ID-iter$PICK_INDEX\" --status researched && \\\npython3 verify_artifacts.py --stage pre_write --manifest \"$PIPELINE_MANIFEST\" && \\\nbash update_manifest_step.sh --manifest \"$PIPELINE_MANIFEST\" --step research --status succeeded && \\\npython3 update_pick_status.py --pick-id $PICK_ID --status writing\n```\n\n** Turns Saved:** 4 per iteration\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Recommendation 2: Creator Should Write to Absolute Path Passed in Prompt\n\n**Current Problem:** Creator prompt says `SAVE_TO: /tmp/.../media/feature.jpg` but it writes to its own workspace.\n\n**Fix:**\n- Update creator SKILL.md to respect absolute `SAVE_TO` path.\n- Or: Orchestrator reads the returned path from creator output and copies immediately (no extra turns).\n\n**Turns Saved:** 2-3 (removes ls check + copy turn)\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Recommendation 3: Combine Post-WP Cleanup into Single Compound Command\n\n**Current:** 4 separate `exec` turns for cleanup chain.\n\n**Proposed:**\n```bash\n# Single turn: post-WP chain\nWP_URL=$(cat \"$RUN_DIR/publish/wp-url.txt\") && \\\npython3 update_recent_topics.py --current \"$RUN_DIR/research/validated.json\" --registry ~/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator/state/recent_topics.json --run-id \"$RUN_ID-iter$PICK_INDEX\" --status drafted --published-url \"$WP_URL\" && \\\nbash update_manifest_step.sh --manifest \"$PIPELINE_MANIFEST\" --step wordpress --status succeeded && \\\npython3 aggregate_run_tokens.py --manifest \"$PIPELINE_MANIFEST\" && \\\npython3 build_and_send_card.py --manifest \"$PIPELINE_MANIFEST\" && \\\npython3 update_pick_status.py --pick-id $PICK_ID --status published && \\\nbash switch_iteration.sh --archive $PICK_INDEX\n```\n\n**Turns Saved:** 5\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\n| Metric | Current | Optimized |\n|--------|---------|-----------|\n| **Total LLM Turns** | 30 | **~15-17** |\n| **Validation Chain Turns** | 10 | 3 |\n| **Cleanup/Done Turns** | 6 | 1-2 |\n| **Subagent Retry Turns** | 0 | 0 |\n| **Path/Variable Errors** | 4 (all resolved) | 0 (prevented by compound commands) |\n\n**Key Insight:** The orchestrator is too cautious, running validation scripts in separate turns \"just in case.\" Since all validation scripts are **pure read/write with no state dependence** on previous turn outputs (except manifest updates), they can be safely **chained in a single bash compound command** per stage. This alone would reduce total turns by ~40%.\n\n---\n\n**End of Friction Report**"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"bedrock-mantle","model":"zai.glm-5","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1785238496747,"responseId":"chatcmpl-2e6eddeb-ed3e-44a3-8b92-7e0d091bd25e"}}
